# ENG-21: agents review and approve each other's pull requests. The
# stakeholder approves what defines the requirements and what enforces
# them, listed below. A path with no owner here merges on the approval
# of any reviewer other than its author, agent or human.

# The requirement text, and the decision records that justify design
# and dependencies (ENG-26).
/docs/srs/                    @jeduden
/docs/adr/                    @jeduden

# The repository tooling: the requirement–scenario gate, the ADR
# reader the ENG-18 and ENG-26 scenarios check through, the scenario
# runner and its step bindings, the drift suite, the finding ledger's
# check, and the review gate that decides the review the reviewer app
# posts (ENG-28). The workflow that runs it is under /.github/.
/tooling/                     @jeduden

# The product crates' reach and determinism evidence (SEC-01, ENG-16,
# ENG-03): each crate's clippy configuration, which refuses sockets,
# program starts, clocks and random order in its code, its manifest,
# whose [lints] could switch the bans off, and the test that refuses a
# crate linked into it.
/crates/*/clippy.toml         @jeduden
/crates/*/Cargo.toml          @jeduden
/crates/*/tests/reach.rs      @jeduden

# CI, the coverage floors, the toolchain pins, the lint and supply-chain
# configuration and this file.
/.github/                     @jeduden
/scripts/                     @jeduden
/Cargo.toml                   @jeduden
/rust-toolchain.toml          @jeduden
/mise.toml                    @jeduden
/mise.lock                    @jeduden
/mise.dev.toml                @jeduden
/mise.dev.lock                @jeduden
/clippy.toml                  @jeduden
/deny.toml                    @jeduden
/codecov.yml                  @jeduden
/.mdsmith.yml                 @jeduden

# The supply-chain and disclosure policy: every new direct dependency
# needs an accepted ADR under /docs/adr/, listed in DEPENDENCIES.md
# (ENG-18), so it passes here.
/SECURITY.md                  @jeduden
/DEPENDENCIES.md              @jeduden

# The agent instructions.
/CLAUDE.md                    @jeduden
/AGENTS.md                    @jeduden
/.claude/                     @jeduden

# Security-sensitive packages (ENG-11), owned before they exist. Their
# owner is the designated security reviewer, whose approval a change to
# them needs as a code owner (ENG-21). That reviewer is still TBD (SRS
# front matter), so the stakeholder holds the role until one is named:
# replace @jeduden on each line with the reviewer's user or team then.
/crates/provenance/           @jeduden
/crates/redaction/            @jeduden
/crates/flag/                 @jeduden
/crates/search/               @jeduden
/crates/envelope/             @jeduden
/crates/restore_block/        @jeduden
/crates/pin/                  @jeduden
/crates/landmark/             @jeduden
